# `#[controller]`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

Declares a controller component. HTTP controllers own a base path and receive route methods from inherent `#[handlers]` implementations. A controller with `ws = Protocol` instead receives `#[message]` methods for that WebSocket protocol. Import it through the facade:

```rust
use upwell::axum::prelude::*;

#[controller(path = "/users")]
struct UsersController;
```

## Syntax

```rust
#[controller(
    // ordinary component keys,
    path = "/base",
    routes_slice = ControllerRoutes,
    middleware = [RequireUser, AuditRequest],
    ws = Protocol,
)]
struct Controller;
```

The attribute applies only to a struct. It accepts the normal component declaration keys as well as these controller keys:

| Key | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `path = "..."` | HTTP base path. Every HTTP route is joined below it. The default is the empty path. |
| `routes_slice = Name` | Name of the controller's route registry. The default is `{Controller}Routes`. `#[handlers]` blocks targeting a custom registry must use the same `routes_slice = Name`. |
| `middleware = [Type, ...]` | DI-backed `AxumMiddleware` singleton components applied to all HTTP routes. The first entry is outermost; controller middleware is inside application middleware and outside route middleware. |
| `ws = Protocol` | Selects the WebSocket-controller surface for a `WebsocketProtocol` instead of the HTTP-controller surface. |

Controllers are always singleton components. A non-singleton scope is rejected. `path`, `routes_slice`, and controller middleware describe HTTP routing; do not combine them as a substitute for a WebSocket endpoint. WebSocket mounting is configured on the Axum app builder with the protocol's `register_ws` API.

## Containment

`#[controller]` establishes the target type for one or more inherent `#[handlers]` blocks. An HTTP `#[handlers]` block may contain route markers; a WebSocket `#[handlers(ws = Protocol)]` block may contain `#[message]` markers and must name the same protocol selected by `ws = Protocol` here. A marker outside that containment is an error.

## Generated artifacts

For HTTP, the expansion provides component metadata, a `Controller` implementation, a `ControllerDescriptor` in the controller discovery slice, and the per-controller route registry. The generated router resolves the singleton once from the application runtime, mounts every collected handler under the base path, and retains static `HttpRouteDescriptor` metadata. `Axum::auto_discover()` can discover these descriptors.

With the `client` feature of the Axum macro crate, route collection also produces `{Controller}Client<C>` and typed methods for routes whose request and response shape can be represented by the client. Native router and descriptor output is native-only.

For WebSocket controllers, the generated surface is a WebSocket controller descriptor and message registration metadata rather than an Axum HTTP router. Duplicate destinations for the selected protocol are rejected during preparation.

## Features

Use the `upwell::axum` facade rather than direct macro-crate paths. HTTP server registration is native-only. Generated HTTP clients require the macro crate's `client` feature. A WebSocket controller additionally requires the Axum WebSocket support and a registered endpoint for its selected protocol.
